<title>SINGAPORE: Yemen sells 3Q crude - table of volume awarded.</title>
<headline>Yemen sells 3Q crude - table of volume awarded.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yemen has concluded the term sale of third-quarter crude, selling 115,000 barrels per day (bpd) of Masila and 40,000 bpd of Marib.</p>
<p>The following table lists the volume of crude awarded to oil companies in barrels per day and is based on information from various industry sources.</p>
<p>    MASILA:				 MARIB LIGHT:</p>
<p>    Total	15,000     Arcadia	10,000</p>
<p>    Arcadia		  15,000     Total	  10,000</p>
<p>    Mitsui	10,000     Japan Energy  5,000</p>
<p>    BP		10,000     BP		5,000</p>
<p>    Yukong    10,000     ENOC	    5,000</p>
<p>    Statoil    10,000     Mitsui	  5,000</p>
<p>    Vitol		     5,000     TOTAL	  40,000</p>
<p>Japan Energy 5,000</p>
<p>    Kanematsu    5,000</p>
<p>    Phibro	   5,000</p>
<p>    Cosmo	  5,000</p>
<p>    Neste	 5,000</p>
<p>    ENOC			5,000</p>
<p>    Glencore		  5,000</p>
<p>    Coastal	 5,000</p>
<p>    TOTAL		   115,000</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65 870 3080)</p>
</text>
